From: René Rebe <rene@exactcode.de>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ps3disk: restore bounce buffer offset increment

Commit 6e0a48552b8c ("ps3disk: use memcpy_{from,to}_bvec") converted the
scatter/gather helper to the newer bvec accessors and lost the offset
increment in the process. Every bio vector in a multi-segment request is
therefore copied to or from the start of the bounce buffer, corrupting all
but the first.

Single-segment requests are unaffected, so the superblock and small reads
succeed while anything larger returns repeated data. On ext4 this surfaces
as group descriptor and block bitmap inconsistencies, and as binaries that
exist on disk but fail to execute with varying errno between boots.

Fixes: 6e0a48552b8c ("ps3disk: use memcpy_{from,to}_bvec")

Applied here against 6.4. Upstream version posted to linux-block in
November 2025 and reviewed by Christoph Hellwig.
---
 drivers/block/ps3disk.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/block/ps3disk.c
+++ b/drivers/block/ps3disk.c
@@ -84,6 +84,8 @@ static void ps3disk_scatter_gather(struct ps3_storage_device *dev,
 			memcpy_from_bvec(dev->bounce_buf + offset, &bvec);
 		else
 			memcpy_to_bvec(&bvec, dev->bounce_buf + offset);
+
+		offset += bvec.bv_len;
 	}
 }
 
